# Read only by a "docker build" that uses tests/Dockerfile. ci.build.sh builds the test image with the Dockerfile of
# @jahia/cypress (env.Dockerfile), and BuildKit then reads env.Dockerfile.dockerignore next to it, not this file.
# .env is not excluded on purpose: inside the Cypress container, the env.run.sh and env.provision.sh of
# @jahia/cypress source .env (else .env.example, which would replace the values docker-compose passes with
# placeholders) for MODULE_ID and the other values that docker-compose.yml does not pass. artifacts/ holds the
# module jar that env.provision.sh installs from inside the container.
results/
run-artifacts/
node_modules
